{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## PROVEN ROOT CAUSE (runtime-confirmed, not read off the source)\n\n`tests/external/live_jira_dc/conftest.py:127-149` `wait_for_jira_dc_ready` returns on the FIRST\n`/rest/api/2/serverInfo` 200 and **never queries `/rest/api/2/field` at all**. `_REQUIRED_FIELDS`\n(`conftest.py:383`) is only consulted much later, by `_assert_project_capabilities`\n(`conftest.py:466-482`), long after readiness has been declared.\n\n**Discriminating experiment (runtime, stubbed transport).** Loaded the harness conftest by path,\nreplaced `_request` with a stub answering `serverInfo -> 200` and `/rest/api/2/field -> 200` with a\nSYSTEM-ONLY inventory (no `customfield_*`), then called `wait_for_jira_dc_ready(timeout=30)`:\n\n```\nRESULT: wait_for_jira_dc_ready RETURNED (declared READY)\npaths polled: ['/rest/api/2/serverInfo']\nmissing required fields at the moment it declared ready: ['Epic Link', 'Epic Name']\n```\n\n`paths polled` is the discriminator: it rules out \"it checks fields but the check is too lenient\"\nand \"it depends on ordering/timing\". The gate is structurally blind to the field inventory. This\nis exactly the state the probe measured live on run 30944211742 (serverInfo green at 8m32s; 27\nsystem-only fields one second later, `scripts/jira_dc_epic_link_clear_probe.py:131-149`).\n\n**Legitimacy: defect.** The behaviour violates an in-repo contract, not merely an expectation:\n`_assert_project_capabilities` asserts `_REQUIRED_FIELDS` as a hard precondition, and the readiness\ngate that runs before it does not establish that precondition. Gerrit 1387 (`3922f20d09`) already\naccepted this as a defect on the probe path; the harness path was left behind, which is what AC4\nnow measures as drift.\n\n**Caller sweep.** `wait_for_jira_dc_ready` has exactly one caller — the session fixture\n`_jira_dc_harness_ready` (`conftest.py:292`) — plus prose in `tests/external/live_jira_dc/README.md:105-111`.\n`_await_named_fields` has one caller, the probe's `main()`. No caller depends on the current weak\nbehaviour; every caller wants \"usable instance\". Local, low blast radius.\n\n## FIX PLAN\n\n1. **New shared module `scripts/jira_dc_field_readiness.py`** — the ONE readiness definition:\n   `REQUIRED_FIELDS = (\"Epic Link\", \"Epic Name\")`, the bounded budget/interval constants, a pure\n   predicate `missing_required_fields(status, body, names)` (an unusable or system-only inventory\n   yields \"missing\", i.e. NOT ready — never \"degraded image\"), a self-diagnosing\n   `describe_inventory(status, body)`, and a transport-injected poll `await_required_fields(request, ...)`.\n   Both tiers call it, so they cannot drift (AC4). Placed in `scripts/` because `tests/unit` already\n   imports `scripts/` modules widely and the probe workflow runs `python scripts/...` with no venv.\n2. **Harness** — `wait_for_jira_dc_ready` keeps the cheap `serverInfo` poll as its first gate, then\n   waits on `await_required_fields` under its own bounded budget, raising with the observed\n   inventory on expiry (AC1, AC2).\n3. **Probe** — `_await_named_fields` delegates to the shared module (AC4).\n4. **AC3** — `_assert_project_capabilities` routes its field check through the same bounded wait, so\n   the abort message can state that the names never registered within the budget and distinguish\n   \"not registered yet\" from \"not offered by this image\" instead of jumping to an image degrade.\n5. **AC5, the load-bearing negative test** — a system-only field inventory must read as NOT ready,\n   asserted through `wait_for_jira_dc_ready` itself (not just the predicate), plus a positive\n   control and a no-drift test pinning that both tiers use the shared definition.\n\nThe workflow-level curl loops stay as the cheap first gate, per the ticket."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785896105021496001,"uuid":"dfeb1c2a-2ca6-430e-a44c-1ce5f54af31d"}